{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Take the book of the Torah.</b> Midrash: On that day, the seventh of Adar, before the death of Moses our teacher, he wrote thirteen Torah scrolls — for the twelve tribes — and called each tribe one by one and rebuked them and warned them concerning the Torah and the commandments, men by themselves and women by themselves. And he said to them: Take heed, all of you, concerning this book of the Torah that I am giving you, to keep and to do. And one Torah scroll he took and placed it beside the Ark of the Covenant, as it is said: ״לקוח את ספר התורה הזה ושמתם אותו מצד ארון ברית ה׳״. And some say that Gabriel descended and took the Torah from the hand of Moses and brought it up to the Great Sanhedrin on High — this was to make known the righteousness of Moses in the heavenly academy, as it is said: ״צדקת ה׳ עשה״ etc. And not only that, but the righteous on high read from it on Mondays and Thursdays and on Sabbaths and on New Moons and Festivals. In the first chapter of Bava Batra, Rabbi Meir and Rabbi Yehudah disagree: one says the Torah scroll lay inside the Ark, and one says at its side, etc., as is stated there."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:01:40.761883066Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}